# Charas -- a pinch of black resin rubbed off a living plant and rolled between the palms.
#
# Redrawn 2026-09-14. Generated art, not Warlon Mhite's hand: edit freely.
#
# ## Why it is not a small hashish
#
# Hashish is pressed, so it is a slab. Charas is never pressed -- it is hand-rolled and sticky -- so
# it is one smooth tilted roll with a crumb pulled off it: vanilla's resin clump is the same grammar,
# resin as an organic glossy clump. The family is three forms before it is three colours.
#
# Near-black with a warm lit side, because resin taken off a living plant oxidises as it forms. It is
# wet-looking, so it gets the only hard specular in the family besides rosin's: two glints up-left
# and one on the crumb. Items are high contrast, so even a black item runs its full ramp.

@palette default
. = none
1 = 070504      the rim, and the shadow side
2 = 16100B      rim, lit side
4 = 2B2118      the body -- the strain entry's own colour
5 = 3D2E21
6 = 5E4630      the lit face, up-left
7 = 8E6E4B      glints
8 = D6BC93      the wet specular: one pixel

@texture item/charas 16x16 type=item
